{"author":{"id":"673e1e1b6fccff4da5524407c8a8cdc7caf18221aabb93f2bb36ffef5c2a95e8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1779825258,"nonce":"Eo8RrnQGbSwMAPgujAwjpCVxja4=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOSn4-Gc8AAAABDdWRdw","github-url":"https://github.com/kanya-approve/karpenter-provider-rackspace-spot/issues/9","origin":"github"},"title":"Rackspace CCM overwrites Karpenter well-known labels post-registration","message":"Observed on the real-cluster MVP smoke test in \\`hkg-hkg-1\\`.\n\nWe set the well-known Karpenter labels in \\`pool.CustomLabels\\` and they correctly propagate to kubelet \\`--node-labels\\` on first registration — verified on a joining Node:\n\n- \\`karpenter.sh/nodepool=default\\`        ✓ survives\n- \\`karpenter.sh/capacity-type=spot\\`      ✓ survives\n- \\`karpenter.sh/registered=true\\`         ✓ survives (set by Karpenter)\n- \\`karpenter.sh/initialized=true\\`        ✓ survives (set by Karpenter)\n- \\`karpenter.rackspace.com/*\\`            ✓ survives\n- \\`topology.kubernetes.io/zone\\`          ✓ survives (kept as \\`hkg-hkg-1\\`)\n- \\`node.kubernetes.io/instance-type\\`     ✗ **clobbered** to \\`compute1-4\\` (the underlying OpenStack VM SKU)\n- \\`topology.kubernetes.io/region\\`        ✗ **clobbered** to \\`HKG\\` (vs. our \\`hkg-hkg-1\\`)\n\nThe clobber happens after registration completes. Source is most likely the OpenStack cloud-controller-manager (\\`failure-domain.beta.kubernetes.io/region=HKG\\` shows up at the same time, classic OpenStack CCM signal).\n\n### Why it doesn't break the MVP (yet)\n\nKarpenter's binding uses \\`spec.providerID\\` match plus the \\`karpenter.sh/*\\` labels, all of which survive. Pods schedule. The CCM doesn't touch \\`karpenter.sh/*\\`.\n\n### Why it'll matter later\n\n- **\\`node.kubernetes.io/instance-type=compute1-4\\`** is wrong from Karpenter's POV — it expects the ServerClass name (e.g. \\`ch.vs1.medium-hkg\\`). Drift detection and consolidation scoring that read this label will misbehave (treat the node as a different instance type than its NodeClaim claims).\n- Workloads that use \\`nodeSelector\\` or affinity on \\`node.kubernetes.io/instance-type\\` to target a ServerClass will silently miss our nodes.\n- Region label mismatch is mostly cosmetic but causes confusing \\`kubectl describe\\` output.\n\n### Approaches\n\n1. **Defensive patcher controller** (similar to \\`nodelink\\`): watch our managed Nodes, re-apply \\`node.kubernetes.io/instance-type\\` and \\`topology.kubernetes.io/region\\` from the Node's \\`karpenter.rackspace.com/nodeclaim-uid\\` → NodeClaim → \\`Status.NodeName\\` mapping. Will fight the CCM unless we win the last-write race.\n2. **Tell Rackspace** their CCM should leave these alone when set by \\`--node-labels\\` — or expose a setting to disable CCM label management.\n3. **Accept it** and document that users must filter on \\`karpenter.sh/*\\` labels instead of the well-known instance-type label.\n\nProbably (1) is the right MVP fix; (2) is the right long-term fix.","files":null}]}